Z||000000||penetrator||08-30-99||07:42 PM||||When my car gets hot, its stalls when i stops at trafficlights. Then i discovered that the hose on the opposite side, on the inner side of engine (The other part of PCV Valve i think, the air inlet)was lose. Then i put the hose back in the rubber hole and tighten it. But after a week it started to stall when it gets hot, again ? And the hose is in right place, in the rubber hole. Please Help. <br>(i couldent find any answers about my problems in the topic list)<p>Thanks<br>Magnus
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-31-99||08:21 AM||||Sounds like it could be a bad idle air control (IAC) valve to me.  Does the car idle normally when it's cold?
Z||000002||theogre||08-31-99||08:48 AM||||key phrase.... stalls when hot stopping for light..... I'm guessing it's an automatic.<p>TCC lockup solinoid. Unplug the electrical connector on the front of the tranny and see if it stops doing it. If it stops,,, the TCC lock solinoid is hosed. You can replace it yourself with the tranny in the car. Solinoid is under the side cover of the tranny.
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-31-99||02:03 PM||||I didn't even think of that!  (I'm a stick-shift guy.)<p>I almost got a good-running rust-free 91 Cutlass Calais for $500 because it had this same solenoid lockup problem.  In the manual, it looks like a difficult but not impossible fix for a shadetree mechanic.  But the guy traded it in at the dealer for $300 before my wife would give me the OK to buy it.  ARRRRRRGH
Z||000004||stsmithgt||09-01-99||12:33 PM||||I still have the same problem in my 86 GT.  I pull off the freeway and the sucker will want to die waiting at a street light.  I took it in to a friend, which happened to be a service Manager at a pontiac dealership in Sacramento, and found out my automatic Idle controll was messing up, and an EGR sensor not the valve was bad.  They also said my fuel pump is possibly adding to the problem by having a hard time keeping the presure up.  I haven't had time to replace that yet.  Unfortunatly I live down in monterey where the Dealership in sand city refuses to work on Fieros.  What the hell is up with that?  I'm hoping the pump will last another trip up to Sacramento where they know a nice car when they see one. Good luck with yours!)
Z||000005||stsmithgt||09-01-99||12:35 PM||||Oh yeah! It cost 280.00 for the parts and labor for the AIC and EGR.  It'll be another 110.00 to replace the fuel pump P$L.
